Pharmaceutical regulations exist precisely because history shows that without oversight, the most catastrophic harms occur — thalidomide, DES, leaded petrol.
The 'precautionary principle' is not anti-science — it is the recognition that some failure modes are irreversible and warrant special caution before deployment at scale.
Biosafety Level 4 laboratories and dual-use research oversight already regulate dangerous pathogens; genetic engineering warrants equivalent institutional oversight.
